# jaaOS — LITE profile (Debian 13 "trixie", amd64). Used by build/mklive.sh for the live ISO.
# Goal: a small, console-first jaaOS that boots from USB/ISO on BIOS and UEFI machines.
# build/mklive.sh also installs build/profiles/cluster.packages (Docker, mDNS, fzf) on top.
# One package per line; # starts a comment. mmdebstrap installs WITHOUT Recommends, so every
# runtime need is listed explicitly.
#
# Left out on purpose, compared with minimal.packages (those packages are what make the full
# image big):
#   - vendor firmware blobs (firmware-*), CPU microcode -> opt in with FIRMWARE=1
#     (adds build/profiles/lite-firmware.packages)
#   - systemd-ukify (pulls in Python), systemd-boot, sbsigntool, tpm2-tools, efibootmgr:
#     the signed-UKI disk image (build/mkimage.sh) needs these; a live ISO does not
#   - snapper, apparmor-utils (pulls in Python), apparmor-profiles, bluez
# Docs, man pages and non-English translations are excluded at install time (see mklive.sh).

# --- kernel + live boot ---
linux-image-amd64
live-boot
live-boot-initramfs-tools
initramfs-tools
zstd

# --- init / core system ---
systemd
systemd-sysv
systemd-resolved
systemd-timesyncd
systemd-zram-generator
udev
dbus
locales

# --- disks / crypto (enough to open and repair a jaaOS install) ---
cryptsetup
btrfs-progs
dosfstools

# --- networking (wired; WiFi also needs FIRMWARE=1 on most hardware) ---
network-manager
wpasupplicant
iproute2
netbase
iputils-ping
nftables
openssh-server
ca-certificates
debian-archive-keyring
curl

# --- hardening ---
apparmor
auditd

# --- installer (sudo jaa-install): partitioning + base system download ---
gdisk
parted
mmdebstrap
whiptail

# --- base userland ---
sudo
bash-completion
less
vim-tiny
nano
htop
pciutils
